1. Product in one paragraph

A junior developer (or a Jira webhook) submits a ticket. The system: scores story completeness against history and asks the BA specific questions if it's underspecified → decomposes it into work packages typed by Avaloq source type → retrieves precedent tickets on two axes (intent similarity × implementation overlap) and pulls their commit diffs as templates → produces an evidence-cited change plan where every change AND every omission cites a precedent, a dependency edge, or a knowledge-card rule → generates the code delta on top of the precedent diff → compiles in a sandbox and runs generated utPLSQL tests, self-correcting up to 3 iterations → opens a PR for Gate 1 (human code review) → on approval, merges and deploys to a test environment → runs UAT auto-review mapping each acceptance criterion to a test with evidence and a reasoned verdict → Gate 2 (human sign-off) → closes the Jira ticket and indexes it as a new precedent (learning loop). Low confidence, retry exhaustion, or missing knowledge escalate to a tech lead with a full trace. A floating "Avaloq Mentor" chat is available on every screen.

2. Tech stack (fixed — do not substitute)


Frontend: React 18 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + framer-motion. Single SPA. lucide-react icons. No component library.
Backend: Python 3.11 + FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + SQLite (file copilot.db). Async workers via asyncio tasks. Live updates via SSE (/api/events/stream).
Workflow engine: build a small DB-backed durable state machine (tables in §6): every transition is an appended event; on process restart, in-flight tickets resume from their persisted state. Add a comment in code noting Temporal/equivalent as the production replacement.
LLM adapter: Anthropic Messages API (claude-sonnet-4-5 default, model name in env). Mock adapter returns deterministic, seed-driven responses so the app works without a key.
Monorepo: frontend/, backend/, root README.md with one-command startup (make dev or docker compose up), DECISIONS.md.


