4. The workflow (state machine) — implement exactly

States: AI_READY → ANALYZING → (NEEDS_INFO ⇄ ANALYZING) → PLANNING → (AWAITING_DOCS ⇄ PLANNING) → AGENT_CODING → GATE1_REVIEW → DEPLOY_TEST → UAT_REVIEW → GATE2_SIGNOFF → DONE, plus ESCALATED (reachable from PLANNING and AGENT_CODING).

Transition rules:


ANALYZING: completeness score < 0.7 → NEEDS_INFO with specific generated questions posted as (mock) Jira comments; BA answer re-scores.
PLANNING: any work package implicating a source type with no knowledge card → AWAITING_DOCS; user pastes doc text → backend distills it into a new card (LLM adapter) → resume. A plan may only leave PLANNING when every CHANGE and every OMIT row has a citation (§7.3). No evidence path → ESCALATED.
AGENT_CODING: loop generate → compile (sandbox adapter) → run utPLSQL (sandbox adapter) → on failure feed exact error back, retry, max 3 iterations → success opens (mock) PR → GATE1_REVIEW. Exhaustion → ESCALATED with full failure trace.
GATE1_REVIEW: UI Approve → merge + DEPLOY_TEST; Request changes (with comment) → back to AGENT_CODING with the comment in worker context.
UAT_REVIEW: build per-criterion verdicts (§7.5) → GATE2_SIGNOFF. Sign-off → DONE: close mock Jira ticket, index the ticket as a new precedent (it must appear in future retrievals), update co-change stats.
Every state change: append event row + publish SSE + mirror to mock Jira (status + comment).
Confidence is computed per work package (§7.4); the ticket state advances with the slowest package; amber/low packages are flagged, not blocking, except < 0.60 before coding → that package escalates.


