7. Backend behavior specs

7.1 API (all under /api)

POST /tickets/analyze (paste text or pick fixture id) · GET /tickets · GET /tickets/{id} (full drill-down: packages, matches, plan, iterations, tests, uat, events) · POST /tickets/{id}/answer (BA answer) · POST /tickets/{id}/docs (paste doc → card) · POST /tickets/{id}/gate1 {decision, comment} · POST /tickets/{id}/gate2 {decision} · POST /tickets/{id}/escalation/ack · GET /fleet · GET /actions (action queue) · GET /knowledge · POST /mentor (chat) · GET /events/stream (SSE) · GET /stats (landing metrics).

7.2 Retrieval (two axes)

Intent similarity: embed story text (LLM adapter provides embed(); mock returns precomputed vectors from fixtures) → cosine vs. past tickets. Implementation overlap: Jaccard over touched (source, field) sets from the ticket-code graph in fixtures. Return top-3 with both scores + the precedent's diff. Axis disagreement (high intent, low overlap) must lower confidence and produce a plan note.

7.3 Evidence rules (the Source-Necessity Reasoner) — enforce in code, not prompt

A plan_item is invalid unless evidence_type + evidence_ref resolve to: a precedent match ≥ 0.70 intent, a dependency edge present in the fixture graph, or an existing knowledge card rule. OMIT rows require evidence too (e.g., epic scope note) and set needs_confirmation=true. An unresolvable needed source → create ASK row → AWAITING_DOCS. Unit-test these rules directly.

7.4 Confidence

confidence = 0.35*intent_sim + 0.20*impl_agreement + 0.20*pattern_support + 0.15*card_coverage + 0.10*execution_health, recomputed after each iteration. Bands: ≥ 0.85 green (auto-proceed), 0.60–0.84 amber (proceed, flagged at Gate 1 with listed reasons), < 0.60 red (escalate before coding). Store the component breakdown for UI display.

7.5 UAT auto-review

For each acceptance criterion: design a test (LLM adapter; mock uses fixture mapping), "execute" via sandbox adapter (mock returns seeded evidence), verdict PASS/FAIL with reasoning, or MANUAL if not automatable — never drop a criterion. Persist evidence refs into the evidence store.

7.6 Mentor chat

POST /mentor calls LLM adapter with a system prompt: senior Avaloq mentor, answers grounded in the source catalog + knowledge cards, cites card names, says "I don't have a card for that — paste the doc and I'll learn it" when unknown. Mock adapter has 6+ canned Q&A from fixtures.

8. Adapter interfaces (adapters/base.py)


JiraAdapter: get_ticket, post_comment, transition, on_webhook (mock: fixtures + in-memory; real: jira lib stub).
BitbucketAdapter: create_branch, open_pr, merge (mock: records PRs, generates plausible diff refs).
SandboxAdapter: compile(delta) -> CompileResult, run_tests(suite) -> TestResults, deploy_test_env, run_uat_probe. Mock behavior: driven by fixture script — for the golden ticket, iteration 1 compile fails with a realistic Avaloq/PLSQL error, iteration 2 passes, tests pass; for the escalation ticket, all 3 iterations fail.
LLMAdapter: complete(system, messages), embed(text). Real: Anthropic SDK. Mock: deterministic fixture-driven outputs (plans, deltas, explanations, UAT designs, mentor answers).


