12. Build order


Backend skeleton: models, state machine + event log + resume-on-boot, SSE, seed loader. 2. Mock adapters + pipeline workers for the golden path through Gate 1. 3. Evidence rules + confidence engine + unit tests (§13). 4. Frontend design system primitives, then frames 1–4. 5. Frames 6–8 wired to gates. 6. UAT stage + frame 9; learning write-back. 7. Frames 10–11, escalation + AWAITING_DOCS flows, mentor chat. 8. Durability test (§11.11), polish pass against §5, README.


13. Definition of done


Full demo script §11 passes manually; a pytest suite covers: every legal/illegal state transition, evidence-rule rejection cases (plan item without citation must raise), confidence bands, retry cap → escalation, learning write-back (new precedent retrievable), evidence-store hash chain integrity.
npm run build clean, mypy clean, no console errors, empty states designed (no blank screens), all times/dates real, README explains mock vs. real adapter config (.env.example included).
Visual check against §5: near-white background, one gradient in exactly two uses, pill buttons, monospace chips, frosted nav + chat, generous whitespace. If it looks like a dense enterprise dashboard, redo the offending screen.


